@startuml auth-flow
title Authentication flow: week3_miniProject_with_HTML\n(as implemented today)

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC

actor "Staff user" as User
participant "Browser page\n(searchPatient / addEncounter /\nupdatePatientDetails .html)" as Page
participant "config.js" as Config
participant "FastAPI app\n(main.py)" as API
participant "CORSMiddleware" as CORS
participant "service.py" as Service
participant "repository.py" as Repo
participant "database.py" as DB
participant ".env\n(DATABASE_URL)" as Env
database "PostgreSQL\n(fde_DRIQ)" as PG

== Server start-up ==
API -> DB : import (via service -> repository)
DB -> Env : load_dotenv(); os.getenv("DATABASE_URL")
Env --> DB : postgresql://<user>:<password>@host/db
note right of DB
  The full connection string, password included,
  is printed to the console:
  print('connection string:', DATABASE_URL)
end note

== Any request (e.g. PATCH /interventions/{encounter_id}) ==
User -> Page : open page, fill in form\n(no login screen exists)
Page -> Config : read window.API_BASE
Config --> Page : http://127.0.0.1:8001
Page -> API : fetch(API_BASE + path)\nheaders: Content-Type only\n(no Authorization header, no cookie)
API -> CORS : check Origin
note right of CORS
  allow_origins=["*"], allow_credentials=True,
  allow_methods=["*"], allow_headers=["*"]
  -> every website is allowed
end note
CORS --> API : allowed

note over API
  **No authentication step.**
  No Depends(), no API key, no token or session check.
  All 9 endpoints, including POST /encounters and
  PATCH /interventions/{id}, run for any caller.
end note

API -> Service : patch_care_intervention(...)
Service -> Repo : update_care_intervention(...)
Repo -> DB : get_connection()
DB -> PG : psycopg.connect(DATABASE_URL)
note right of PG
  **The only credential check in the app:**
  Postgres verifies the user/password in DATABASE_URL.
  Every request runs as that single database user,
  never as the person using the page.
end note

alt credentials valid
  PG --> DB : connection
  DB --> Repo : conn
  Repo -> PG : UPDATE care_interventions ...
  note right of PG
    Database permissions (sql/createUser.sql):
    care_management, hospital_operations,
    clinical_leadership, finance_transformation
    may SELECT both tables; only care_management may
    UPDATE intervention_status, assigned_to, notes,
    updated_at. These apply only if DATABASE_URL
    signs in as one of those users.
  end note
  PG --> Repo : rowcount
  Repo --> Service : True / False
  Service --> API : success, or ValueError
  API --> Page : 200 {"success": true}\nor 400 error
else credentials invalid / DB down
  PG --> DB : connection error
  DB --> Repo : None (error printed)
  Repo --> Service : False
  Service --> API : ValueError
  API --> Page : 400 "Failed to update care intervention..."
end

Page --> User : show result
@enduml
